WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.310
The last part ended on a worry.

2
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.290
A lawn is small.

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.390
The big problems are real, and people need help now.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.990
If no one is forced, how does anything get solved?

5
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.050
Fair enough.

6
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:20.250
So take the hardest case there is, and hear the objection at full strength.

7
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.950
You cannot talk a man out of your garage at two in the morning.

8
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.690
You cannot pass the hat for every victim in a city.

9
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.470
Some problems need the police, the courts and the prison,

10
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.850
and everyone has to pay for them, whether they want to or not.

11
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.750
Ruth's beans are one thing.

12
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.670
A burglary is another.

13
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.072
Now do crime.

14
00:00:41.972 --> 00:00:45.132
Start with the system the objection trusts.

15
00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:49.292
One night in August someone pries open Dan's garage.

16
00:00:49.292 --> 00:00:54.112
In the morning the ladder is still on its hooks, but the tool chest is gone,

17
00:00:54.112 --> 00:00:56.372
and a rebuilt engine with it.

18
00:00:56.372 --> 00:00:59.752
Dan drives to the station and fills out a report.

19
00:00:59.752 --> 00:01:01.272
The officer is polite.

20
00:01:01.272 --> 00:01:03.612
He gives Dan a case number.

21
00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:06.649
And that is the last Dan ever hears of it.

22
00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:09.089
Dan is not unlucky.

23
00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:10.869
He is typical.

24
00:01:10.869 --> 00:01:15.709
An earlier part gave one number: of every hundred thefts and break-ins in this

25
00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:19.129
country, about four end with anyone caught.

26
00:01:19.129 --> 00:01:24.569
Violent crime does better, but not by much: about fifteen in a hundred.

27
00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:29.489
Meanwhile the system holds nearly two million people in prisons and jails,

28
00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:33.989
at about forty-four thousand dollars a year each in the federal system.

29
00:01:33.989 --> 00:01:35.789
And the person who was robbed?

30
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:40.009
Federal courts order offenders to pay their victims back.

31
00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:44.409
At last count a hundred and ten billion dollars of that was unpaid,

32
00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:49.249
and a hundred billion of it written off, because the offenders cannot pay.

33
00:01:49.249 --> 00:01:51.810
Dan's tool chest is in that pile.

34
00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.730
Now hold that against something you already know.

35
00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.510
Every problem is solved with time, talent and money,

36
00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:03.590
and there are three ways to gather them: share your own,

37
00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.930
persuade others to join you, or force them.

38
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.950
Force is not a result.

39
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.730
It is a way of gathering.

40
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:16.130
And for crime, this is what forcing everyone to pay has gathered: a system that

41
00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.630
catches almost no one, cages the few it catches at great expense,

42
00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:23.270
and leaves the victim with nothing.

43
00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:26.810
Nobody here is arguing against stopping a burglar.

44
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.056
The question is what the method is actually buying.

45
00:02:30.956 --> 00:02:34.236
So go back to a line from earlier in this series.

46
00:02:34.236 --> 00:02:38.556
Someone who takes by force owes a debt to the person they took from.

47
00:02:38.556 --> 00:02:39.936
Not to the public.

48
00:02:39.936 --> 00:02:41.116
To Dan.

49
00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:45.336
The young man who emptied Dan's garage owes Dan a tool chest,

50
00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:47.856
a garage door and a bad month.

51
00:02:47.856 --> 00:02:52.186
The question that matters is not how many years he should sit in a cell at

52
00:02:52.186 --> 00:02:54.116
forty-four thousand dollars each.

53
00:02:54.116 --> 00:02:58.317
It is how Dan gets made whole, and how the young man stops.

54
00:02:59.217 --> 00:03:01.757
This already has a name and a room.

55
00:03:01.757 --> 00:03:04.147
The young man is caught.

56
00:03:04.147 --> 00:03:06.497
Nineteen, a first offense.

57
00:03:06.497 --> 00:03:10.037
Instead of a courtroom, he sits at a table.

58
00:03:10.037 --> 00:03:12.057
His mother is beside him.

59
00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:16.697
Dan is across from him, and Ruth, because Dan asked her to come.

60
00:03:16.697 --> 00:03:19.317
A trained facilitator runs it.

61
00:03:19.317 --> 00:03:23.097
Dan says what it cost him, and not only in dollars.

62
00:03:23.097 --> 00:03:26.757
The young man hears it from the person, not from a prosecutor.

63
00:03:26.757 --> 00:03:30.757
Then they work out what he owes and how he pays it.

64
00:03:30.757 --> 00:03:33.877
Dan gets his tools, or the money for them.

65
00:03:33.877 --> 00:03:37.029
The young man gets a debt he can actually finish paying.

66
00:03:37.929 --> 00:03:40.169
Does it hold up past one table?

67
00:03:40.169 --> 00:03:44.829
New Zealand has used this for nearly every young offender in the country since

68
00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:49.909
1989, and the person harmed is invited every time.

69
00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:54.049
In the first year, nine conferences in ten reached an agreement,

70
00:03:54.049 --> 00:03:57.909
and most of those young people never saw a courtroom.

71
00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:03.049
In ten controlled trials, offenders who met the person they harmed went on to

72
00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:07.929
commit fewer crimes, and the effect was largest for violent crime.

73
00:04:07.929 --> 00:04:12.189
The victims came away more satisfied, less set on revenge,

74
00:04:12.189 --> 00:04:14.509
and with fewer symptoms of trauma.

75
00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:17.249
The drop in reoffending is modest.

76
00:04:17.249 --> 00:04:19.560
What it does for the victim is not.

77
00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.680
And notice what the table does that the cell cannot.

78
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.320
An earlier part said your greatest protection from other people is the other

79
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.740
people's values.

80
00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.380
A cell holds a man for a term and works on nothing inside him.

81
00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.220
Two out of three are arrested again within three years.

82
00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.934
The table works on the value itself.

83
00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:45.374
Now the honest part, because the skeptic has earned it.

84
00:04:45.374 --> 00:04:49.474
New Zealand's conferences run inside a government system.

85
00:04:49.474 --> 00:04:53.394
Nobody has yet shown the voluntary way at the scale of a nation,

86
00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:56.014
and the philosophy does not claim it.

87
00:04:56.014 --> 00:04:58.474
What it claims is narrower.

88
00:04:58.474 --> 00:05:02.794
Force is a method, and the method should carry the burden of proof.

89
00:05:02.794 --> 00:05:06.294
Where the voluntary way has been tried, measure it.

90
00:05:06.294 --> 00:05:08.354
Where it works, use more of it.

91
00:05:08.354 --> 00:05:13.634
Where it has not been shown, say so, and prove it before you spread it.

92
00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:17.171
Nobody is asked to trade a life for a theory.

93
00:05:18.071 --> 00:05:19.631
One last look at Dan.

94
00:05:19.631 --> 00:05:23.591
Two years ago he never crossed the road to talk to Ruth.

95
00:05:23.591 --> 00:05:28.551
This fall he sat across a table from the young man who robbed him, and talked,

96
00:05:28.551 --> 00:05:31.749
and the tools came back a payment at a time.

97
00:05:32.649 --> 00:05:35.709
Which leaves a question that is harder than it sounds.

98
00:05:35.709 --> 00:05:38.989
Who decides when the voluntary way is ready?

99
00:05:38.989 --> 00:05:44.469
And until then, whose values get enforced: yours, or your neighbor's?

100
00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:47.769
That is next: The Method Is the Message.

101
00:05:47.769 --> 00:05:51.803
The whole series, in order, is at humanrespect.app.
